{"results":[{"id":"W2052218930","title":"The Pen Is Mightier Than the Keyboard: Advantages of Longhand Over Laptop Note Taking","year":2014,"snippet":"In three experiments, students who took longhand notes performed better on conceptual questions than those who used laptops, but review was not manipulated."},{"id":"W2964123456","title":"Note-taking mode and review: Testing the encoding and external-storage functions of note taking","year":2019,"snippet":"Across two experiments, handwritten and laptop note takers either reviewed or did not review their notes before a test; review improved performance similarly in both modes."},{"id":"W3001122334","title":"The effects of longhand versus laptop note taking on learning: A meta-analysis","year":2021,"snippet":"Meta-analysis found a small longhand advantage for conceptual learning, with no evidence that review moderated the effect."},{"id":"W3123456789","title":"Reviewing handwritten versus typed notes: Does mode matter for later recall?","year":2020,"snippet":"Reviewing notes improved recall, but the benefit did not differ between handwritten and typed notes."}]}
