{"id":"W2964123456","title":"Note-taking mode and review: Testing the encoding and external-storage functions of note taking","year":2019,"abstract":"Two experiments examined whether reviewing notes moderates the effects of note-taking mode. In Experiment 1, undergraduates took notes either longhand or on a laptop and then either reviewed or did not review their notes before a conceptual test. Reviewing notes improved test performance, but the improvement was similar for longhand and laptop note takers; the mode-by-review interaction was not significant. Experiment 2 replicated this pattern with a delayed recall test. These findings suggest that note review does not change the relative effectiveness of handwritten versus laptop note taking."}
</tool_response>
