{"id":"W3001122334","title":"The effects of longhand versus laptop note taking on learning: A meta-analysis","year":2021,"abstract":"This meta-analysis synthesized studies comparing longhand and laptop note taking. Longhand note taking was associated with a small advantage for conceptual learning. Moderator analyses found no evidence that whether students reviewed their notes moderated the longhand advantage. The results indicate that the small longhand benefit is not conditional on note review."}
</tool_response>
